//! A browser shell's words on an `iframe` (LLP 1020.002): what `contract
//! vocab` says of each, beside its row, prop or event.

/// The note for an attribute or event of a browser shell's `iframe`.
pub(super) fn note(name: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
    Some(match name {
        "partition" => "on an `iframe`: `persist:<name>` (1 to 64 of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -) keeps the guest's cookies and storage across launches, `<name>` keeps them in memory for the session; every frame naming one partition shares them. The guest is a top-level page, as a browser tab is: no `sandbox`, no `message=` and no `postMessage`, and only http(s) or about:blank sources. macOS and iOS honour it; on the web the frame is an ordinary `<iframe>` and `exactPage().iframePartition` is false, so read that first to choose a fallback. On Apple the frame events and commands are a partitioned frame's. Clear one with `clearSiteData` from `@exact/browser`; data code may call it only when the Contract names the send (`send m = clearSiteData(…)`, LLP 1133.002 D14) (LLP 1020.002 D1, D4)",
        "zoom" => "CSS `zoom`, on an `iframe` only: the frame's own lengths grow by it and its guest's page is zoomed by it (`pageZoom` on Apple), as Chrome zooms a frame; a frame sized by its container keeps its size (LLP 1020.002 D6)",
        "apple.allowsBackForwardNavigationGestures" => "`WKWebView.allowsBackForwardNavigationGestures` on an `iframe`; unsaid, false, WebKit's default; inert on other platforms (LLP 1020.002 §9)",
        "apple.allowsMagnification" => "macOS `WKWebView.allowsMagnification` on an `iframe`; unsaid, false; inert elsewhere (LLP 1020.002 §9)",
        "apple.inactiveSchedulingPolicy" => "`WKPreferences.inactiveSchedulingPolicy` on an `iframe`: \"suspend\", \"throttle\" or \"none\"; unsaid, \"throttle\" for a partitioned frame (a hidden tab keeps running, throttled) and WebKit's default, \"suspend\", otherwise, which suspends the page about 4 minutes after its window is covered, or seconds after launch in a window never shown, so a page that keeps a socket open while hidden says \"throttle\"; inert elsewhere (LLP 1020.002 §9, \"Stage 1 as built\")",
        "currententrychange" => "on an `iframe`: the guest's document committed, or its title, icons or history changed with no navigation; the `FrameNavigation` record says what it shows now (LLP 1020.002 D2)",
        "navigatesuccess" => "on an `iframe`: the guest's navigation finished loading; every navigation ends in this or `navigateerror` (LLP 1020.002 D2)",
        "navigateerror" => "on an `iframe`: the guest's navigation failed, was stopped (`AbortError`) or refused (`NotSupportedError`), or its content process died (`crashed`, with `recovering` while another reload follows) (LLP 1020.002 D2)",
        "newwindow" => "on an `iframe`: its guest asked for a window, with a `FrameNewWindow` record: a `new-window` (`window.open` with features, ⇧-click) has already opened as the platform's popup, a window (macOS) or a sheet (iOS) in the same partition, so OAuth's `postMessage` to its opener works; a `foreground-tab` or `background-tab` (`target=_blank`, ⌘-click, middle click, `window.open` without features) opens nothing, so the app opens a tab or calls `openURL`. A frame without it opens nothing. A scripted window needs a person's gesture, `about:blank` is refused, a POST to a new tab loads in the frame itself, and a URL that is not http(s) gets the platform's confirmation before its app opens, never this event. macOS and iOS; on the web the browser opens its own windows and this never fires (LLP 1020.002 D5)",
        "download" => "on an `iframe`: a download its guest started (a response WebKit cannot show, `Content-Disposition: attachment`, `<a download>`), with a `FrameDownload` record as it goes: `progressing` once it starts, then `completed` (with `path`), `cancelled` (no place was chosen) or `interrupted`. Unsaid, the platform asks where to save (a save panel on macOS; the export picker on iOS once it finishes). macOS and iOS; on the web the browser downloads on its own and this never fires (LLP 1020.002 D5)",
        "FrameNewWindow" => "an `iframe` guest's window request: `url`, and `disposition`, Electron's name for it: `new-window` (the platform's popup opened), `foreground-tab` or `background-tab` (nothing opened; the app's to open) (LLP 1020.002 D5)",
        "FrameDownload" => "a download an `iframe`'s guest started: `url`, `suggestedFilename`, `state` (Electron's `DownloadItem` states: `progressing`, `completed`, `cancelled`, `interrupted`) and `path`, the saved file once `completed` (an `app:/` path under the agent's default, otherwise the place the person chose) (LLP 1020.002 D5)",
        "capture" => "on an `iframe`: the answer to `captureScreenshot`, with a `FrameCapture` record: `path` (the `app:/` path the command named, which ties the answer to its request), `width` and `height` (the PNG's pixels), or `error` (a DOMException name) and `message`. macOS and iOS; on the web it answers `NotSupportedError`, since a page cannot read a frame's pixels (LLP 1020.002 D7)",
        "userpromptopened" => "on an `iframe`: a dialog (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`) of a frame that `@exact/browser-automation` drives, with a `FrameUserPrompt` record; no sheet is shown, and data code answers it with `handleUserPrompt`. Once a person's input reaches the frame, the dialog is shown to them as the platform's sheet. macOS and iOS; on the web the browser shows its own (LLP 1020.002 D9)",
        "FrameUserPrompt" => "an agent-controlled `iframe`'s dialog, by WebDriver BiDi's `browsingContext.userPromptOpened`: `type` (`alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`), `message`, and `defaultValue` (a prompt's default text) (LLP 1020.002 D9)",
        "FrameCapture" => "the answer to an `iframe`'s `captureScreenshot`: `path` (the `app:/` path it named), `width` and `height` (the PNG's pixels: the clip's size in view points times the screen's scale), `error` (\"\" when the file was written; otherwise a DOMException name: `NotSupportedError` on the web, `IndexSizeError` for a clip outside the viewport, `InvalidStateError` for a frame with no box, `UnknownError` for a failed write) and `message` (LLP 1020.002 D7)",
        "DOMRect" => "Geometry's `DOMRect`, built as `DOMRect(x=…, y=…, width=…, height=…)`: a rectangle, as `getBoundingClientRect()` gives one; an `iframe` capture's `clip=`, in the guest's CSS pixels relative to its viewport (LLP 1020.002 D7)",
        "navigate" => "on an `iframe`: the guest began a navigation (a link, a script, `navigate(id, url)`, a redirect), its `FrameNavigation` record's `destination` set; on the navigation root it is a location from outside the app",
        "FrameNavigation" => "the Navigation API's names for what an `iframe`'s guest shows, seen from outside: `url` (committed), `destination` (in flight), `navigationId`, `navigationType` (push, replace, reload, traverse), `title`, `icons` (candidate URLs, then /favicon.ico), `canGoBack`, `canGoForward`, `loading`, `partitioned`, `controller`, and for `navigateerror` `error`, `message` and `recovering`. On Apple only a partitioned frame reports them; on the web a same-origin frame does, one that leaves the page's origin ends in `navigateerror` (`NotSupportedError`), and a cross-origin guest reports `load` only (LLP 1020.002 D2, §11)",
        _ => return None,
    })
}

/// A frame command's text after "host command".
pub(super) fn command(name: &str) -> Option<&'static str> {
    Some(match name {
        "navigate" => "; `navigate(\"frame-id\", url)` loads an http(s) URL or about:blank in that partitioned `iframe`, the Navigation API's `navigation.navigate(url)`; another app's scheme (`mailto:`) gets the platform's confirmation before that app opens, and `javascript:`, `file:`, `data:` and `blob:` are refused (LLP 1020.002 D3, D5)",
        "traverseHistory" => "; `traverseHistory(\"frame-id\", delta)` moves that partitioned `iframe` through its history, -1 back and 1 forward, as `history.go(delta)`; with no entry there it fires `navigateerror` with `InvalidStateError` (WebDriver BiDi's `browsingContext.traverseHistory`, LLP 1020.002 D3)",
        "reload" => "; bare `reload()` boots the app again (the development host's Reload); `reload(\"frame-id\")` reloads that partitioned `iframe`'s page, `reload(\"frame-id\", ignoreCache=true)` revalidates it end to end (LLP 1020.002 D3)",
        "stopLoading" => "; `stopLoading(\"frame-id\")` stops that partitioned `iframe`'s navigation in flight, which ends in `navigateerror` with `AbortError` (`WKWebView.stopLoading()`, LLP 1020.002 D3)",
        "captureScreenshot" => "; `captureScreenshot(\"frame-id\", \"app:/tmp/shot.png\")` writes a PNG of that `iframe`'s guest as it shows now, and `clip=DOMRect(x=…, y=…, width=…, height=…)` a part of it, in the guest's CSS pixels relative to its viewport (a `getBoundingClientRect()`), as a pinch or pan leaves it; the frame answers with `capture=` (WebDriver BiDi's `browsingContext.captureScreenshot`; macOS and iOS, any `iframe`, a PDF one too; `NotSupportedError` on the web; LLP 1020.002 D7)",
        "openDevTools" => "; `openDevTools(\"frame-id\")` opens the platform's inspector for that `iframe`'s guest in a window of its own, or brings it to the front when it is open (Electron's `<webview>.openDevTools()`); on macOS that is Safari's Web Inspector, through WebKit's private `_inspector`, and the frame becomes inspectable from Safari › Develop too; iOS makes the frame inspectable from a Mac's Safari › Develop and opens nothing; the web, which has no API for it, refuses it in the log, as does a host with no web view (LLP 1020.002 D11)",
        _ => return None,
    })
}
